%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f73fecfc74277694c85e74139e346573, type: 3}
  m_Name: Tutorial_GettingStarted
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ProjectSpark.AI.Tutorial.SparkTutorialDefinition
  tutorialId: project_spark_first_circuit
  displayName: Build Your First Circuit
  resumeFromCheckpoint: 1
  steps:
  - id: welcome
    title: Meet your AI lab instructor
    explanation: Welcome to ProjectSpark. I'll guide you through the tools, explain
      what the components do, and let you build the circuit yourself.
    hint: You can repeat explanations with F2 and request help with F1.
    conceptId: 
    advance: 0
    requiredSignal: 
    focus: 0
    worldTarget: {fileID: 0}
    screenTarget: {fileID: 0}
    locatorKey: 
    worldOffset: {x: 0, y: 0.05, z: 0}
    autoHintAfterSeconds: 16
    speak: 1
    allowSkip: 1
  - id: resistor_intro
    title: What is a resistor?
    explanation: A resistor limits electric current. Its resistance is measured in
      ohms. A 220-ohm resistor usually passes less current than a 100-ohm resistor
      at the same voltage.
    hint: The colored bands help identify its resistance.
    conceptId: 
    advance: 0
    requiredSignal: 
    focus: 1
    worldTarget: {fileID: 0}
    screenTarget: {fileID: 0}
    locatorKey: shelf.resistor
    worldOffset: {x: 0, y: 0.05, z: 0}
    autoHintAfterSeconds: 16
    speak: 1
    allowSkip: 1
  - id: select
    title: Pick a component
    explanation: Click a resistor in your storage shelf to select it. You can also
      drag it to the workstation.
    hint: Choose an available resistor from the shelf.
    conceptId: 
    advance: 1
    requiredSignal: shelf.item_selected
    focus: 1
    worldTarget: {fileID: 0}
    screenTarget: {fileID: 0}
    locatorKey: shelf.resistor
    worldOffset: {x: 0, y: 0.05, z: 0}
    autoHintAfterSeconds: 16
    speak: 1
    allowSkip: 1
  - id: workstation
    title: Place it on the workstation
    explanation: Place the selected resistor into the resistor workstation slot.
      The shelf manager will verify that the slot is compatible and available.
    hint: Click the empty resistor slot, or drag the resistor over it and release.
    conceptId: 
    advance: 1
    requiredSignal: shelf.item_placed
    focus: 1
    worldTarget: {fileID: 0}
    screenTarget: {fileID: 0}
    locatorKey: workstation.resistor
    worldOffset: {x: 0, y: 0.05, z: 0}
    autoHintAfterSeconds: 16
    speak: 1
    allowSkip: 1
  - id: replace
    title: Move or replace parts
    explanation: To change a resistor, disconnect attached wires first. Drag the
      resistor back to storage, then place a different value in the empty slot.
    hint: Powered or connected parts may be protected from unsafe moves.
    conceptId: 
    advance: 0
    requiredSignal: 
    focus: 1
    worldTarget: {fileID: 0}
    screenTarget: {fileID: 0}
    locatorKey: workstation.resistor
    worldOffset: {x: 0, y: 0.05, z: 0}
    autoHintAfterSeconds: 16
    speak: 1
    allowSkip: 1
  - id: switch
    title: How a switch works
    explanation: A switch opens or closes a conductive path. A closed switch can
      allow current through a complete circuit. An open switch interrupts that path.
    hint: A switch alone doesn't make a circuit work; the full path must be complete.
    conceptId: 
    advance: 0
    requiredSignal: 
    focus: 1
    worldTarget: {fileID: 0}
    screenTarget: {fileID: 0}
    locatorKey: device.switch
    worldOffset: {x: 0, y: 0.05, z: 0}
    autoHintAfterSeconds: 16
    speak: 1
    allowSkip: 1
  - id: wire
    title: Connect the circuit
    explanation: Click one terminal, then the destination terminal, to create a wire.
      Follow the terminals highlighted by your level instructions.
    hint: Only valid terminal combinations will connect.
    conceptId: 
    advance: 1
    requiredSignal: circuit.connection_created
    focus: 1
    worldTarget: {fileID: 0}
    screenTarget: {fileID: 0}
    locatorKey: terminal.start
    worldOffset: {x: 0, y: 0.05, z: 0}
    autoHintAfterSeconds: 16
    speak: 1
    allowSkip: 1
  - id: current
    title: Voltage, current and power
    explanation: Voltage is electrical potential difference. Current is charge flow.
      For an ideal resistor, I equals V divided by R, and dissipated power is I squared
      times R.
    hint: Too much dissipated power can overheat and damage a resistor.
    conceptId: 
    advance: 0
    requiredSignal: 
    focus: 0
    worldTarget: {fileID: 0}
    screenTarget: {fileID: 0}
    locatorKey: 
    worldOffset: {x: 0, y: 0.05, z: 0}
    autoHintAfterSeconds: 16
    speak: 1
    allowSkip: 1
  - id: finish
    title: You're ready to experiment
    explanation: You know how to select, place and replace parts, what resistors
      and switches do, and how to begin wiring. Try the level objective. Ask the
      AI instructor for help whenever needed.
    hint: You can revisit this tutorial from your Help menu.
    conceptId: 
    advance: 0
    requiredSignal: 
    focus: 0
    worldTarget: {fileID: 0}
    screenTarget: {fileID: 0}
    locatorKey: 
    worldOffset: {x: 0, y: 0.05, z: 0}
    autoHintAfterSeconds: 16
    speak: 1
    allowSkip: 1
